EmailTemplate.textOnly:
{!Contact.FirstName},

I wanted to check in and see where you were at with getting the account back on track.  Because the account is so far past due, it is slated to be removed from our active loan files at the end of the month. This means it will be reported as defaulted to business credit that may impact your ability to get additional financing.  The file will also be sent to the litigation team for evaluation, which may include the filing of a lawsuit against you and the business.

I would like to help you avoid this by setting up a schedule to resume payments that may require a payment to be made before the end of the month. Is that something you can do at this time?

Please let me know.
Thank you,

{!Case.Case_Email_Signature_Name_Formula__c}

National Funding, Inc., the parent and servicing company of
Quick Bridge Funding, LLC

{!$Setup.Company_Information__c.Street__c}
{!$Setup.Company_Information__c.City__c}, {!$Setup.Company_Information__c.State__c} {!$Setup.Company_Information__c.Zip__c}
P: {!Case.OwnerPhone}

